WEBVTT

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:21.270
This story is a work of fiction. All persons and organizations are imagined. 
The kabaddi and game rules which appear in this anime are drawn from the original work.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.120
Oh! So this is where you were, Yoigoshi!

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.330
Azemichi.

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:22.910
I went and borrowed the key from Senpai.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:25.540
Let's get to the gym early 
and start practicing!

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:29.420
I've got no problems with that, but...

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:30.970
Is that guy a friend of yours?

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.730
<b>Membership Application</b>

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:17.800
<i>Team
\h\h\h\h\hApplicants</i>

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:18.490
<b>Membership Application</b>

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:17.920
His name's Ban Nobutaka! 
He says he wants to join the team!

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:23.900
Once you talk to him, 
turns out he's a pretty good guy!

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:26.170
It's true we're looking for members, but...

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:27.540
Huh?

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:32.630
<b>I want to give it a try, too!</b>

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:32.630
His voice is so quiet!

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:35.080
We can't let a guy like him join!

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:37.340
But he says he wants to.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:40.510
He's so scary, it'll make it 
hard for anyone else to join.

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:43.510
We should put him on hold 
until we gather more members.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:45.640
<b>After School</b>

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:49.140
Excuse us!

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:50.090
Huh?

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:53.690
Huh? This is the kabaddi team, isn't it?

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:56.970
We'd like to join, you see. 
Ban-kun told us about it.

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:00.600
You threatened them, didn't you?!

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:03.160
<b></b>I didn't threaten them.

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:04.460
Talk louder!

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.140
He said he didn't threaten them.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:07.410
How can you hear him?

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:11.120
Um, you see, it was Ban who invited us.

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:13.900
That's how we ended up going 
to watch your practice match.

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:17.840
As we watched, we got so fired up.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:20.130
We thought it looked like a lot of fun.

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:20.760
And that's why...

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:24.370
I'm a first-year. My name's Hitomi. 
I hope you'll let me join!

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.880
No, no, no, no, no...

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:28.270
We don't have enough 
members to need a manager.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:32.810
There's nothing!

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:35.190
I'm a boy.

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:37.820
I thought I might be able to 
become a little more manly here.

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:42.450
M-Maybe you should try cutting 
your hair shorter or something.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:44.570
My hair is like this due 
to family circumstances...

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:50.140
"A man doesn't change through appearance, 
but through what's inside."

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:52.270
Is what he said. I feel the same way.

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:54.260
Seriously, what is up with the two of you?

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:56.220
And you there...

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:58.390
First-year, Class 6. My name is Seki.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.100
How much do you weigh?

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:01.900
85 kilos.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:05.050
You can't participate in tournaments 
if you're over 80 kilos.

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:08.680
Come on. He's saying he wants to do it.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:12.540
He'll be the one getting hurt 
and crying if we lose, too.

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:17.150
He's just the kind of person 
Ban-kun said he was.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:18.230
Huh?

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:20.900
I was wondering, do you remember Ban?

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:22.150
I don't know him.

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:28.170
I guess it's fine. I'll check all 
of you out before our senpai arrive.

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:32.040
I'll raid. You guys defend.

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:36.210
You have to run so Yoigoshi 
can't touch you. Okay?

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:37.500
Yes, sir!

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:40.990
If you're hopeless, our senpai 
aren't going to want you!

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:42.830
It's dangerous, so you just watch once!

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:43.760
Yes, sir!

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:46.650
And you've gotta be careful he 
doesn't cross the bonus line.

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:47.680
Understood.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:50.780
And if you see your chance, 
you've gotta go for it!

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:50.430
<b>He's completely forgotten...</b>

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:51.930
Roger!

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:57.750
<i>I feel like he's got it 
in for me for some reason.</i>

00:04:58.170 --> 00:04:59.130
Okay, here I come!

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:00.610
Okay!

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:03.930
<i>So, he doesn't remember.</i>

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:08.460
<i>We met during summer vacation
 in second grade.</i>

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:11.090
That looks great on you, Ban!

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:14.330
We've got a soccer game later, 
so you should come to the school.

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:16.620
The other team's definitely gonna freak out!

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:21.130
For being such a coward, 
Ban's sure got a scary face!

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:23.160
Later!

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:40.640
<i>All the people who pushed me around got 
pushed around themselves by one lone man.</i>

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:45.780
What? Is this all you've got?

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:50.090
<i>I remember that it was a very hot day.</i>

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:54.290
<i>Without even thinking, 
I spoke to him before I left.</i>

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:57.340
Whoa! Your hair's insane!

00:05:57.340 --> 00:05:59.490
Oh. They forced me to...

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:01.330
It stands out. I'm jealous!

00:06:01.330 --> 00:06:02.800
Huh? Stands out?

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:06.920
There's this player who stands out for 
having a ponytail even though he's a guy.

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:09.310
Standing out means a ton 
more pressure, right?

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:12.810
But he makes awesome plays and gets 
results in spite of it. He's so cool!

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:15.370
I truly admire him!

00:06:16.590 --> 00:06:20.280
<i>From that day on, 
Yoigoshi-san became the one I admired.</i>

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:23.730
<i>I started playing soccer.</i>

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:28.380
<i>Whenever time allowed, I'd follow 
Yoigoshi-san's games and practices.</i>

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:32.110
<i>He started to speak less and less.</i>

00:06:32.110 --> 00:06:35.240
<i>Even as Yoigoshi-san stopped smiling 
as he played, I followed him.</i>

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:40.680
<i>And kept following until I heard 
he'd quit sports entirely.</i>

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:46.630
<i>But... I...</i>

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:54.960
<i>I always believed...</i>

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:01.540
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:02.740
<i>Welcome back.</i>

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:06.360
<i>Even if it's only a little...</i>

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:08.860
<i>I want to get closer to you!</i>

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:10.160
<i>This guy!</i>

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:10.930
Kabaddi?!

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:12.360
<i>What's with those eyes?</i>

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:14.450
You're wide open!

00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:15.940
Kabaddi!

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:21.350
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:21.350
<i>No way I'm letting a gang 
of rookies take me out!</i>

00:07:21.350 --> 00:07:23.380
Only just started

00:07:21.350 --> 00:07:23.380
<b>A Rookie</b>

00:07:21.350 --> 00:07:23.380
<i>A rookie who has only just started.</i>

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:26.060
<i>I have to show these beginners how it's done!</i>

00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:28.550
Joined team 2 months ago

00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:28.550
<b>A Beginner</b>

00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:28.550
<i>A beginner who joined 
the team two months ago.</i>

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:34.720
This does, indeed, seem 
to be a dangerous sport.

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:38.550
It would probably be best 
for me to remove my glasses.

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:41.690
Have you played sports before?

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:45.210
Ah! I was on the sumo team 
through middle school.

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:46.880
Really?

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:47.360
Huh?

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:48.760
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:50.320
What do you think you're doing?

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:52.360
He wanted to touch you, Yoigoshi-san.

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:54.490
Oh, me, too!

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:55.370
What?

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:57.960
I really admire muscles.

00:07:58.970 --> 00:08:00.880
Would you mind if I touched them?

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:04.970
Uh, well... I wouldn't mind... exactly...

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:07.540
I've never seen Yoigoshi like this before.

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:08.860
No one asked you!

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:10.010
Anyway! These guys are—

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:13.680
Looks like we've got quite 
a wide reach, senpai!

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:17.420
They're team applicants. Nice to meet you.

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:20.270
Kei! A round one! There's a round one!

00:08:21.090 --> 00:08:23.390
If you get taken down in a three-on-one 
with beginners, then...

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:27.670
I'm the captain, Ojo! Are you hoping to join?

00:08:27.670 --> 00:08:29.270
Y-Yes, sir!

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:30.410
Glad to have you!

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:35.190
<i>And thus, new friends 
joined the kabaddi team.</i>

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:40.540
There are only three months left 
until the tournament in August.

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:44.000
First, let's build a team that 
can win the first round, okay?

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:45.080
Sir!

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:46.380
<b>\h\hSir!\h\h</b>

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:50.230
But, to think you've always 
lost the first round.

00:08:50.230 --> 00:08:51.800
That's because...

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:55.330
Iura-senpai's luck at the 
draw is beyond terrible.

00:08:55.330 --> 00:08:57.390
So, today we will decide your positions!

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:58.860
<i>He glossed over it!</i>

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:03.890
Def.

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:03.890
Raider

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:02.860
In the tournament, we'll play seven-on-seven.

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:05.830
The defensive positions are 
groups of two, three, and two.

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:10.150
Def.

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:10.150
Raider

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:10.150
Usually, these three groups each 
form chains and move independently.

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:12.720
<i>So, this is like announcing 
the starting lineup.</i>

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:15.070
We'll start in positions that 
make it easy to attack the raider.

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:21.120
<b>Def.</b>

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:17.560
Left Corner, Yoigoshi.

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:19.910
Right Corner, Cap.

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:24.650
You'll have the same role 
as me. I'll teach you.

00:09:24.650 --> 00:09:25.700
Sir.

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:27.890
Next, the center three.

00:09:27.890 --> 00:09:29.220
Left Cover, Misumi.

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:30.410
Sure thing!

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:31.810
Center Man, Date.

00:09:31.810 --> 00:09:32.770
Yes, sir!

00:09:32.770 --> 00:09:34.010
Right Cover, Ban.

00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:37.650
That's amazing, Ban-kun!

00:09:37.650 --> 00:09:41.220
Ban's 180 cm tall and 
he has soccer experience.

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:43.760
The data indicates he has 
decent athletic ability.

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:46.060
Wh-Where did you get that kind of data?

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:50.780
For now, it seems we have no choice but 
to ask Hitomi to use his head to fight.

00:09:50.780 --> 00:09:51.830
I'll do everything I can.

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:54.630
Next to Cap, the Right In will be me.

00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:57.740
Azemichi will be Left, next to Yoigoshi.

00:09:59.190 --> 00:10:00.240
Yes, sir!

00:10:00.550 --> 00:10:04.750
Since Seki has experience in sumo, 
he's got speed and power.

00:10:05.390 --> 00:10:07.150
And his height's about 
the same as Azemichi's.

00:10:08.940 --> 00:10:11.250
N-No, it's much too early for me to...

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:14.180
Then, you'll have to try switching in for me!

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:16.440
Having strong members is best, 
after all, right?

00:10:16.850 --> 00:10:17.530
Yes.

00:10:20.630 --> 00:10:22.730
<i>He's as softhearted as always.</i>

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:33.610
<b></b>Kabaddi... Kabaddi...

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:47.940
Thanks for letting us leave before you!

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:50.440
I'm going, then.

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:51.630
See you later.

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:55.810
My bottom hurts. Does it look swollen?

00:10:55.810 --> 00:10:59.630
Don't worry about it. You just need 
to put on more muscle, Hitomi-chan.

00:11:00.270 --> 00:11:03.310
Yeah. Seems like everyone's 
going to work out well for us.

00:11:03.790 --> 00:11:06.350
Players with sports experience 
tend to do well.

00:11:06.590 --> 00:11:08.700
For now, we've got to teach 
them what we can.

00:11:09.910 --> 00:11:10.810
Senpai!

00:11:11.570 --> 00:11:14.020
Would you be willing to train with me?

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:19.280
You've been staying late every day,
 but you don't have to push so hard.

00:11:19.630 --> 00:11:22.720
In terms of ability, you'll end up
 on the starting lineup, Soma.

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:27.410
In a real match, you can't even exhibit a 
third of what you've achieved in training.

00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:30.240
That's why I'll do three times, no...

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:33.650
I want to do even more than that.

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:37.080
All right.

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:40.800
Captain, what about me?

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:42.790
Oh... Soma, you're...

00:11:43.540 --> 00:11:46.080
You're doing okay. Just keep 
working hard like this.

00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:53.370
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:11:59.010 --> 00:12:01.690
That was terrible, Soma.

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:04.140
One more time!

00:12:13.340 --> 00:12:15.080
There are two roles in defense!

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:19.390
There are those who stop the raider, 
vanguards in an elite attacking role, Strikers,

00:12:19.820 --> 00:12:23.340
and those who finish the downed 
raider in a support role, Backup.

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:25.100
Let me hear you as we play!

00:12:25.100 --> 00:12:25.900
Sir!

00:12:27.150 --> 00:12:31.480
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:31.480
Here he comes! Everyone keep to your roles!

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:32.420
Strikers!

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:34.090
Backup!

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:36.230
Kabaddi!

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:39.230
Too slow!

00:12:39.950 --> 00:12:40.860
Kabaddi!

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:42.530
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:47.160
<i>He covered for him?</i>

00:12:47.480 --> 00:12:50.120
<i>That's not the way to be kind, Azemichi.</i>

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:55.420
You really are ruthless, but that's 
the kind of role you've got, right?

00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:56.770
Kabaddi!

00:12:56.770 --> 00:12:59.670
But I can't just set things aside.

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:02.880
If my friends are weak, 
I'm going to go save them!

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:05.840
If I'm weak, I'm going to 
ask my friends to teach me!

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:08.710
That's the kind of strength I'm aiming for!

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:10.280
<i>This guy...</i>

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:11.640
Kabaddi—

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:12.730
Backup!

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:15.020
<i>Backup?</i>

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:16.390
Kaba—

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:23.860
You're doing it all yourself!

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:25.860
Date

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:25.860
Misumi

00:13:26.130 --> 00:13:27.860
<b>Team Misumi</b>

00:13:28.130 --> 00:13:29.870
<b>Team Date</b>

00:13:30.270 --> 00:13:34.000
For the next few turns, 
I'll be raiding each team in turn.

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:36.370
The team that loses the fewest points wins.

00:13:36.780 --> 00:13:40.700
Hitomi-kun and Kei will defend for both teams.

00:13:40.700 --> 00:13:43.280
This is a weird kind of intra-squad game.

00:13:43.280 --> 00:13:46.010
<i>No, this isn't an intra-squad game.</i>

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:49.050
Everyone, give it everything you've got...

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:51.440
and stop me!

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:55.370
Kabaddi!

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:09.290
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:14:11.270 --> 00:14:12.600
That's enough for today!

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:15.480
Everyone, check to see 
how many points you lost!

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:15.700
Misumi Team
Score
Misumi
Azemichi
Ban

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:15.700
Date Team
 Score
 Date
 Yoigoshi
 Seki

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:17.080
Date

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:17.080
Misumi

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:16.580
Sir!

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:19.370
We lost by five points!

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:20.490
Thank you!

00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:23.840
<i>That Hitomi...</i>

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:29.840
Misumi Team
Score
Misumi 4
Azemichi 7
Ban 9
Hitomi 13
Iura 2

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:29.840
Date Team
Score
Date 6
Yoigoshi 4
Seki 11
Hitomi 18
Iura 1

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:27.490
On the other team,
 he lost thirteen points,

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:29.710
but on our side,
 he lost eighteen points.

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:33.290
Are you wondering about 
the points Hitomi-kun lost?

00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:35.780
Do you think he might
 be slacking off or something?

00:14:35.780 --> 00:14:37.180
Oh, uh, no!

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:39.350
I don't think I'm doing that, but...

00:14:39.350 --> 00:14:43.440
If you don't know the reason for the 
five-point difference in Hitomi-kun's scores,

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:45.930
that means you don't 
understand each other yet.

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:50.490
Why don't you try hanging out with everyone?

00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:53.850
Hang out? What am I supposed to do?

00:14:53.850 --> 00:14:56.620
<i>A person who has only ever played soccer.</i>

00:14:53.970 --> 00:14:56.700
<b>A person who has
only ever played soccer.</b>

00:14:56.940 --> 00:15:00.420
Hang out, huh? It's not like there are
 any mountains nearby, right?

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:02.880
<i>A person who didn't have 
many places to hang out.</i>

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:02.880
<b>A person who didn't have 
many places to hang out.</b>

00:15:03.150 --> 00:15:04.500
If no one minds...

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:07.050
May I decide what we do?

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:08.510
<i>This guy is good!</i>

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:15.750
Bowling, huh?

00:15:17.010 --> 00:15:19.540
There's wind coming out 
of this weird rack thing!

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:23.780
It feels like throwing this 
would train your core.

00:15:23.780 --> 00:15:25.610
<i>He doesn't know what 
"hanging out" means!</i>

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:28.780
Yoigoshi! Let's have a match!

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:32.090
You think you'll be able to beat me?

00:15:32.090 --> 00:15:33.990
<i>He gets serious super fast!</i>

00:15:34.380 --> 00:15:35.820
It'll be a team match.

00:15:35.820 --> 00:15:38.410
Are we all right with using 
the teams we used in practice?

00:15:38.890 --> 00:15:40.830
The losers buy drinks for everyone!

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:43.210
That vending machine sells ice cream!

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:48.430
He's a little too serious about it, 
but this might work out.

00:15:48.430 --> 00:15:52.340
And you can't help wondering how 
Yoigoshi would do at bowling, right?

00:15:55.490 --> 00:15:56.720
<b>Gutter</b>

00:16:00.540 --> 00:16:01.730
<b>Strike</b>

00:16:02.150 --> 00:16:04.340
All right! I knocked them all down!

00:16:04.340 --> 00:16:05.740
Why can't I knock them down?

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:08.740
Azemichi-kun is better?

00:16:08.740 --> 00:16:10.240
Oh, Ban-kun!

00:16:10.520 --> 00:16:12.470
It might be better to go a little easy on...

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:15.270
There's no need for that?

00:16:20.110 --> 00:16:21.250
Somehow...

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:24.730
the more he throws...

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:31.720
Yeah!

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:33.470
He's amazing!

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:48.360
<b>Today's games have ended.
Thank you for your patronage.
</b>Please press "Enter".

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:52.020
We won!

00:16:52.020 --> 00:16:53.860
B-Blast them!

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:55.860
It's okay. Don't let it bother you.

00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:59.610
Damn it. If I'd just knocked 
down one more pin that time...

00:16:59.610 --> 00:17:02.500
But you knocked down quite 
a lot, Yoigoshi-kun.

00:17:02.710 --> 00:17:07.000
To make up for the shortcomings of my allies,
 I should have worked myself harder.

00:17:07.610 --> 00:17:10.800
But, man, Yoigoshi, you really learn fast.

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:13.100
Maybe it's because there's no 
weird habits in your movement?

00:17:13.100 --> 00:17:16.100
Getting Ban and Hitomi acclimated
 took a lot of work!

00:17:16.100 --> 00:17:18.830
Thanks to Azemichi-kun 
correcting me point by point,

00:17:18.830 --> 00:17:20.540
I got a good score for the first time!

00:17:21.730 --> 00:17:22.980
A good score?

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:30.900
Azemichi Team
Total | Player Name
118            Hitomi
152         Azemichi
131                Ban

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:30.900
Yoigoshi Team
Total | Player Name
98             Hitomi
177           Yoigoshi

00:17:26.240 --> 00:17:29.240
<i>Now that I look, it happened again.
 Hitomi's scores are...</i>

00:17:33.930 --> 00:17:35.550
We'll be going, then!

00:17:35.550 --> 00:17:36.240
Okay!

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:39.220
What should we do?

00:17:39.220 --> 00:17:41.630
I'm hungry, so let's get something to eat.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:45.210
W-W...

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:47.390
Want to grab some food with me?

00:17:57.130 --> 00:17:58.970
What is it about me that doesn't work?

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:01.890
Huh? Where'd this come from?

00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:03.740
<i>They sound like a couple, don't they?</i>

00:18:08.140 --> 00:18:10.080
Maybe the ball you used had 
something wrong with it.

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:12.070
I'm not talking about bowling!

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:16.610
Back in practice, it seems like you 
were able to do well with Azemichi.

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:20.140
Oh! He covered for me 
and gave me directions.

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:23.340
Though, Azemichi-kun lost more 
points because he did that.

00:18:28.260 --> 00:18:31.000
<i>That way of doing things 
really is softhearted.</i>

00:18:31.610 --> 00:18:33.170
I was thinking...

00:18:33.580 --> 00:18:35.910
You're too nice, Yoigoshi-kun.

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:37.570
What?

00:18:37.570 --> 00:18:40.840
You take everything on yourself, 
like earlier, right?

00:18:41.500 --> 00:18:42.810
That was...

00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:46.060
Azemichi-kun makes a lot more demands.

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:49.410
The way Yoigoshi-kun doesn't rely 
on anyone is really amazing, right?

00:18:50.010 --> 00:18:50.930
Right?

00:18:50.930 --> 00:18:51.900
<i>It's not like that...</i>

00:18:52.670 --> 00:18:56.360
<i>I... just didn't trust you, that's all.</i>

00:18:57.530 --> 00:19:01.080
<i>I know that watching strong 
people leads to strength.</i>

00:19:02.030 --> 00:19:04.050
<i>That's why I watched closely and learned.</i>

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:07.470
<i>But looking at it another way, 
I haven't done anything else.</i>

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:13.160
<i>If you don't look, there's no 
way you'll understand, right?</i>

00:19:15.530 --> 00:19:17.030
Then, we'll see you later!

00:19:17.030 --> 00:19:17.770
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:22.000
<i>I thought that as long as I kept growing,</i>

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:24.190
<i>I could make up for the 
shortfalls of my allies.</i>

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:27.440
<i>That in itself isn't a mistake.</i>

00:19:29.010 --> 00:19:31.470
<i>The only one I worked to develop was myself.</i>

00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:35.780
Everyone around me, huh?

00:19:36.980 --> 00:19:39.770
<i>That's way harder than just 
focusing on one person.</i>

00:19:41.570 --> 00:19:44.070
<b>A Few Days Later</b>

00:19:44.070 --> 00:19:46.410
I'll act as a lure, like usual.

00:19:48.770 --> 00:19:50.340
<i>No changes?</i>

00:19:51.640 --> 00:19:54.540
I would have liked to go with Yoigoshi-san...

00:19:52.590 --> 00:19:54.860
Ban says he wishes he'd 
gotten to go eat with you!

00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:56.270
I can't hear you!

00:19:56.270 --> 00:19:57.740
Let's get started!

00:19:57.740 --> 00:19:58.920
Sir!

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:02.180
Then, we'll start with the group 
that lost last time, Date's team.

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:03.040
Yes, sir!

00:20:06.880 --> 00:20:08.090
Kabaddi.

00:20:08.850 --> 00:20:11.120
<i>Everything's going as usual so far.</i>

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:14.270
Kabaddi.

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:17.030
<i>He's gotten used to the way I move.</i>

00:20:17.640 --> 00:20:19.610
<i>Though you can't win just by dodging.</i>

00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:23.300
<i>They don't come in at the 
beginning of the raid!</i>

00:20:23.760 --> 00:20:25.050
<i>Something's different.</i>

00:20:26.110 --> 00:20:27.790
We need to do the unexpected.

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:32.460
Seki, you've got, you know... 
good explosive power.

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:35.130
Make speed your priority 
and go for the captain.

00:20:35.720 --> 00:20:37.180
You think that'll work out okay?

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:39.570
Kabaddi.

00:20:39.570 --> 00:20:41.310
You'll get hit with a counter.

00:20:41.960 --> 00:20:45.760
But after the counter, he'll be 
just a little bit off the ground.

00:20:45.760 --> 00:20:48.510
There will be a moment when 
he can't make any big moves.

00:20:50.830 --> 00:20:51.520
Kabaddi.

00:20:52.330 --> 00:20:53.830
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:20:54.980 --> 00:20:58.860
<i>You have the ability to clearly see 
your enemies and those above you.</i>

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:00.570
<i>I know that.</i>

00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:02.040
<i>But, what's beyond that?</i>

00:21:02.480 --> 00:21:05.910
Hitomi is much slower than we are.

00:21:05.910 --> 00:21:07.990
So, if he goes for a catch 
with the same timing as us,

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:11.620
he'll end up grabbing the 
captain with different timing.

00:21:14.380 --> 00:21:16.370
<i>This is the first time I've 
been the one touching!</i>

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:18.810
Kabaddi... Kaba—

00:21:18.810 --> 00:21:19.690
Backup!

00:21:23.010 --> 00:21:24.630
Kabaddi!

00:21:24.910 --> 00:21:26.130
He used him as a shield?!

00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:30.990
Sorry!

00:21:30.990 --> 00:21:33.350
Huh? Oh, no, I'm fine.

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:34.690
Yoigoshi-kun...

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:39.020
I... I'm really sorry. 
After you took the trouble to...

00:21:39.540 --> 00:21:40.520
If it's possible...

00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:43.080
go for the legs, not the hips.

00:21:43.690 --> 00:21:46.320
And Seki, don't close your eyes.

00:21:46.320 --> 00:21:48.000
It's after the catch that you 
need to use your strength.

00:21:49.050 --> 00:21:49.880
And...

00:21:51.100 --> 00:21:54.310
<b>\hthat wasn't bad.\h</b>

00:21:52.190 --> 00:21:53.660
Huh? What was that?

00:21:55.750 --> 00:21:57.740
Are you Ban or something?

00:21:57.740 --> 00:22:00.420
It's not fair to try to stop 
the cant by making us laugh.

00:22:01.110 --> 00:22:03.850
Kei. Did you give them orders?

00:22:03.850 --> 00:22:06.870
No. I'm in a neutral position right now.

00:22:08.750 --> 00:22:10.970
As captain, I'm happy, but...

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:13.820
for the first time in a long time...

00:22:14.350 --> 00:22:16.410
I feel like I might get taken down.

00:23:48.940 --> 00:23:54.250
<b>Next Time
"A Battle of Wills"</b>

00:23:49.340 --> 00:23:52.420
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:23:50.000 --> 00:23:52.200
Next time, "A Battle of Wills!"

00:23:52.420 --> 00:23:53.250
Kabaddi!
